  ✕ Reference may mutate a value read in the same expression
   ╭─[test.lis:6:18]
 5 │     let mut c = Counter { n: 1 }
 6 │     let _ = bump(&c) + c.n
   ·                  ─┬    ─┬─
   ·                   │     ╰── may see the mutated value
   ·                   ╰── may mutate `c`
 7 │ }
   ╰────
  help: Make evaluation order explicit: to read the value before `&c` runs, copy it first with `let before = c.n`, and to read the value after, bind the reference-taking operand to a variable first · code: [infer.reference_aliases_sibling]
